fflush of a stream reading, as POSIX has it: where the file is capable of
seeking, its offset is set to the stream's position, and what the stream
read ahead or ungetc pushed back is dropped; a file of no position keeps
its offset, and errno. FreeBSD's flushes only what a stream has to write.
fflush with no stream does it to every stream, fclose to its stream, and
exit (_cleanup) to all, so a process leaves each file's offset where its
stream was.

